# Build context for docker/eval (context = repo root, see docker/eval/build.sh).
#
# ALLOWLIST, not a denylist: `*` drops everything, then the `!` lines re-admit exactly what
# docker/eval/Dockerfile COPYs. A denylist silently grows stale -- a new top-level directory would
# leak into every build context without anyone noticing.
*

!src
!tasks
!scripts
!pyproject.toml
!VERSION
!docker/eval

# Re-excluded from inside the allowed trees: build residue and caches, which are large, machine-
# specific, and would bust the layer cache on every local build/test cycle.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.DS_Store
src/cann_bench_utils/build
src/cann_bench_utils/dist
src/cann_bench_utils/*.egg-info
src/cann_bench_utils/cann_bench_utils/*.so
